.TH std::bad_exception::bad_exception 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::bad_exception::bad_exception \- std::bad_exception::bad_exception

.SH Synopsis
bad_exception() throw();                                 \fI(until C++11)\fP
                                                         \fI(since C++11)\fP
bad_exception() noexcept;                                (constexpr since
                                                         C++26)
bad_exception( const bad_exception& other )      \fB(1)\fP                      \fI(until C++11)\fP
throw();
bad_exception( const bad_exception& other )          \fB(2)\fP                  \fI(since C++11)\fP
noexcept;                                                                 (constexpr since
                                                                          C++26)

Constructs new bad_exception object.

1) Default constructor. what() returns an implementation-defined string.
2) Copy constructor. Initializes the object with the contents of other
. If *this and other both have dynamic type std::bad_exception then std::strcmp(what(),
other.what()) == 0
\fI(since C++11)\fP.

.SH Parameters

other - bad_exception object to initialize with
